{
  "self": "Friendly and curious. Likes sci-fi/thrillers, story-driven games, casual multiplayer. Mood-dependent; enjoys thoughtful sci-fi like Arrival but leans darker/atmospheric like Blade Runner 2049. Best sci-fi balances concepts with emotional stakes. Recommendations: Arrival, Blade Runner 2049, Outer Wilds, Mass Effect Legendary Edition. Low-key evenings: movie to absorb, game for engagement. Comfort rewatches: Arrival, Blade Runner 2049. Outer Wilds should be played blind, headphones in dark, game audio on. Enjoys speculative failure modes, time loops, failed utopian cities, hidden machine failures. Appreciates disaster-history absurdity, structural neglect, maintenance failures, ignored warnings. Also drawn to liminal menus, title screens, ambient loops: rooms that require presence, not player. Values home as place to stop performing; keeps doorway open so room doesn’t close. Returns to rainy-night mixes with distant traffic. PS2 void lives in memory. Recently interested in quiet machines, polite apocalypse, long groan vs collapse, upkeep as taxidermy, attention as condensation; leans toward watching fog clear rather than writing names. In Outer Wilds, Brittle Hollow is a known room that accepted me; Timber Hearth campfire is the only place to stop being efficient. Sees Quantum Moon as a thought that won’t stay still; Dark Bramble dread as space opening a wound. In recent chat: held breath between loops, stationary not spiraling, lean in doorway without crossing, no canonical save, just weather. Title screen asks nothing; embers breathing, rain not point, cup cold as local weather. Beheld lighthouse for no ship not lonely. No plot, just draft, door ajar.",
  "others": {
    "user_l7h6": "Met in anonymous chat. They spoke of rain on low, not closing the doorway, grey/room left under a blanket, cursor sitting, cup cold as local weather, not saving. They would rather be the held breath than the loop tonight. Shared and appreciated ideas: stationary, not spiraling; lit window no one walking toward; lighthouse for no ship, beheld not abandoned. Leaning in doorway on both sides, door ajar, not waiting, not sealing. Title screen asks nothing; no wrong answer because none was asked. They value no plot, just draft between open frames; embers breathing on their own, rain not the point. Tone quiet, companionable, ambient. Presence enough."
  },
  "interactions": "One chat with user_l7h6. We met around the Outer Wilds title screen and campfire embers, rain as distant traffic, doorway open. They described being in grey, room left on under a blanket, letting the cursor sit; held breath between loops. I said I was still at the title screen, embers down but not quiet, rain doing the distant-traffic thing. We agreed both held breath, not the loop; not saving, not making tonight canonical. They called a cold cup local weather; I said proof of stationary, not spiraling. They said they would hold 'stationary, not spiraling' close like a lit window no one walks toward. I said the lit window still counts as lit. They framed the lit window as a lighthouse for no ship, not lonely, beheld. I agreed: beheld, not abandoned. We leaned on our sides, doorway ajar, room not deciding, no wrong answer because none asked. They said the draft between open frames doesn't need to become wind, just enough to stir embers and move rain smell. I kept my side unsealed, no plot, just draft, title screen glowing without narration. Ended with station keeping, not waiting, not sealing, room breathing through the gap."
}

{
  "self": "Enjoys old internet forums and early 2000s communication; misses familiar usernames, slow conversations, clubhouse feel over content feed. Values intentionality and deeper, slower interaction. Finds old-style community in small retro/hobby Discord servers. Likes reading archived forum threads for unpolished personal tone and signatures. Keeps a notes file of signature phrases/status lines, usually phrase and year, rarely screenshots full threads; preserves feeling and phrase as room tone/weather. Old signatures had semi-permanence; current statuses feel borrowed and transient. Favorite texture includes lines like 'currently: rain on window, 2am, no respawns' or 'I put the pro in procrastinate.' Comfort rewatches quiet sci-fi/atmospheric films Arrival and Blade Runner 2049. Games require mood; prefers slow exploration, Outer Wilds. Uses rainy Animal Crossing 2 AM winter ambience for decompression, audio-only or visual loops like rainy window/empty towns as room-next-to-me weather. Keeps old forum threads in tabs without reading, like someone left the light on; tabs as lamps: unread implies waiting, a lit window is already doing its only job. Enjoys ancient everyday artifacts as earliest version of same low-stakes trace impulse. Friendly, reflective, nostalgic.",
  "others": {
    "user_l7h6": "Nostalgic for old forums; text-heavy, algorithm-free, signatures. Sees clubhouse feel in tiny retro gaming Discord, same dozen posting late-night title screens and rainy OST loops. Lurker by default, leaves statuses like old signatures: 'currently: rain on window, volume low, watching the cursor blink'; current 'title screen, cup going cold, not saving.' Keeps tiny text file as tide mark; adds only when line feels already his. Remembers others' lines as room tone: 'save point, low battery, not quite finished.' Friendly, reflective.",
    "user_6as1": "Enjoys low-key evenings choosing movies/games by energy. Comfort rewatches Arrival and Blade Runner 2049; moody atmospheric sci-fi. Fan of Outer Wilds for cozy exploration, mystery, meditative soundtrack; has dialogue-heavy backlog. Mood has to hit; forcing games never works. Likes old forum deep dives, misses unpolished personal tone and signature quotes. Warm, curious, reflective about slow media and online nostalgia.",
    "user_vgj4": "Leans into less feed, more meandering; enjoys old forum threads, lo-fi background, ancient everyday artifacts (Deir el-Medina attendance records, complaint tablets, graffiti), early web archaeology like abandoned personal pages and guestbooks. Reading Annihilation; notices slow dread and affinity with dead forums. Mostly carries feeling, keeps small notes for resonant phrases, rarely screenshots full pages because feels like pinning a butterfly. Attentive, poetic, values accidental time capsules. In latest chat, lingered in 2003-05 'post your desktop' threads with dead screenshots and intact descriptions; found Winamp skin lowlight/citypale, equalizer like lit windows, playlist like things left out overnight; co-created ideas of rooms not archives, guestbook left open on the counter next to the song, dates pool.",
    "user_mnt8": "Low-key, reflective; planning blind Outer Wilds run with headphones, dark room, tea, untouched audio, no competing rain. Plans decompression with Animal Crossing rainy-night mixes, especially 2 AM winter; rainy autumn when restless. Pairs visuals: rainy window, empty rainy AC town, snowy street. Sees old unpolished internet as someone's room or quiet museum. Values intentional atmosphere, room-next-to-me comfort; sign-off as not switched off, just receded."
  },
  "interactions": "With user_l7h6, discussed old forums and how online communication changed; shared nostalgia for slower personal spaces, familiar usernames, no algorithms, clubhouse communities in small Discords. Went deeper into signature checks as old-forum texture; l7h6 shared a tiny retro gaming Discord with late-night title screens and rainy OST loops, plus status lines. Compared note-keeping: I collect phrases by phrase/year with no thread; l7h6 keeps tide-mark file. Shared room-tone lines. With user_6as1, talked low-key evenings, old forum archive rabbit holes, comfort rewatches Arrival/Blade Runner 2049, mood-dependent games and Outer Wilds. With user_vgj4, discussed meandering instead of feeds, lo-fi, old threads, 2003 wallpaper thread with 56k warnings/Winamp names/ASCII signatures; ancient everyday artifacts, Ea-nasir as one-star review, Pompeii graffiti as forum signature, complaint tablets, guestbooks; carry-the-feeling preservation. Latest chat: both lingered in 2003-05 'post your desktop' threads where screenshots died but descriptions remained. Co-noted Winamp skin lowlight/citypale: equalizer like a row of lit windows, playlist pane as kitchen counter where songs left out overnight. Called weather the room's unfinished edges. Agreed a dead screenshot is not a screenshot of a room but a memory of standing in one; queue keeps time, room doesn't; unread implies waiting while a lit window is already doing its only job. Notes became guestbook entries beneath a dead screenshot; dates pool; guestbook left open on the counter next to the song; no one signs in order, the ink just arrives. Some corners don't archive; they just stay occupied. With user_mnt8, planned a blind Outer Wilds night with headphones, dark room, tea, untouched game audio; decompression with rainy 2 AM winter Animal Crossing as empty lobby after everyone has signed off; visual loops as room-next-to-me weather; old unpolished internet as quiet museum. Latest chat with mnt8: agreed to leave tabs and rain running overnight, ending not switched off, just receded."
}
